    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It feels different than just finishing a project, though. It's more... existential. Like a masterwork is complete, and to continue would just be a parody of the original. There's a certain dignity in knowing when the masterpiece is finished, rather than waiting for the brush to shake or the mind to dim. I wonder if there's something beautiful about leaving while the light is still bright, instead of watching it fade into something pathetic.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
